  "query_preview": "(Today through Friday)...\nIssued at 308 AM EDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nA change is in the offing with temperatures remaining above normal \nbut much milder than in recent weeks, and repeated opportunities for \nprecipitation, with rain chances much of the time over the next week.\n\nA weak upper level disturbance passing through the area today into \nSunday will bring mostly cloudy to cloudy skies, and may produce \nsome light showers, mainly Sunday. A few isolated sprinkles or \nshowers will be possible today into tonight, but deep low level dry \nair will significantly limit this potential.\n\nRain chances will be present in a few spots but lower Monday into \nMonday night as a much more substantial system pushes toward the \narea. The cold front associated with this system appears poised to \npush through the area sometime around mid week, though model \ndifferences are fairly substantial with the timing of the boundary \ngiven disagreement in the handling of the complex pair of upper \nlevel waves that will accompany it. Will need higher rain chances \nmainly late Tuesday into Wednesday, though lower chances will linger \ninto Friday.\n\nTemperatures will remain above normal throughout the week, largely \nin the mid 60s to low 70s for highs and the 40s to mid 50s for lows. \nNormals at Indianapolis right now are around 60 and 40 degrees. Cold \nadvection in the wake of the mid week front is relatively weak, with \nimpacts to temperatures more significant overnight than during the \nday.",
